## Self-Evaluation – SailPoint IdentityIQ & Identity Security Cloud Developer

## Self-Evaluation – SailPoint IdentityIQ & Identity Security Cloud Developer

During this review period, I continued to apply my technical expertise in SailPoint IdentityIQ to support identity and access management initiatives, application integrations, and ongoing operational needs. I leveraged my knowledge of IIQ architecture, configuration, development, troubleshooting, and integrations to onboard several applications and support business requirements.

A key strength I bring to the team is my depth of knowledge of SailPoint IdentityIQ and my ability to understand how the platform works from both a development and integration perspective. I am able to troubleshoot issues, identify the root cause of technical problems, and determine when a requirement can be supported through configuration or customization versus when there is a platform limitation.

As part of application onboarding, I worked with application teams and stakeholders to understand requirements, configure integrations, address data and provisioning needs, and support testing and implementation. In some cases, I identified IIQ limitations that prevented an application from being onboarded in the manner requested by the business. I communicated those limitations and worked toward practical alternatives rather than implementing solutions that would not be sustainable or supported.

I also continued to expand my knowledge of SailPoint Identity Security Cloud as the organization moves toward more cloud-based identity solutions. While IIQ remains my strongest area of expertise, I have been building my ISC knowledge through hands-on experience, troubleshooting, API and integration work, and learning how ISC differs from the traditional IIQ platform. My goal is to continue developing my ISC expertise to a level comparable to my IIQ knowledge.

From a service delivery perspective, I focus on providing reliable and timely support, maintaining quality in development and configuration, and working collaboratively with application teams and stakeholders. I pay close attention to testing, troubleshooting, and validation to reduce production issues and ensure changes meet requirements before implementation.

I also contribute to Agile delivery by participating in sprint planning, helping clarify technical requirements, identifying dependencies and potential limitations, and breaking larger SailPoint development efforts into manageable tasks. I continue to look for ways to improve planning and make delivery more predictable.

Overall, I believe I have demonstrated strong technical expertise in SailPoint IdentityIQ, a commitment to quality and service, and a willingness to take on new technologies. Going forward, I plan to continue strengthening my SailPoint ISC skills, expanding my cloud and integration knowledge, and contributing to the organization's transition toward modern identity and access management solutions.
